# RB-0021: UniFi Third-Party Gateway Site Repair (Correcting Stale Network Metadata)

**Project:** UniFi Site Separation
**Classification:** Engineering Runbook
**Applies To:**

* UniFi Network Application 10.4.x
* Docker (LinuxServer.io)
* MongoDB 7
* Third-Party Gateway (pfSense / Netgate)
* Self-hosted UniFi Controller

---

# Purpose

Repair a UniFi Site whose displayed network does not match the actual management network after moving devices to a new Site.

Example:

GUI displays

```
192.168.1.0/24
```

Actual network

```
172.16.0.0/24
```

---

# Symptoms

Settings → Networks displays

```
Default
192.168.1.0/24
```

while

```
Switch Management
172.16.0.x

AP
172.16.0.x

Gateway
172.16.0.1
```

Everything functions correctly except the displayed subnet.

