```

Locate the record matching the Site ID.

---

# Step 6 — Export the Record

```bash
docker exec -e MONGO_ROOT_PASS="$MONGO_ROOT_PASS" unifi-db sh -c \
'mongosh --quiet \
--username root \
--authenticationDatabase admin \
--password "$MONGO_ROOT_PASS" \
unifi \
--eval "printjson(
db.networkconf.findOne(
{_id:ObjectId(\"NETWORK_OBJECT_ID\")})
)"'
```

Verify current values.

Example

```
ip_subnet

192.168.1.1/24

dhcpd_start

192.168.1.6

dhcpd_stop

192.168.1.254
```

---

# Step 7 — Stop UniFi

```bash
docker stop unifi-network-application
```

MongoDB remains running.

---

# Step 8 — Update Metadata

Replace

```
NETWORK_OBJECT_ID

SITE_ID
```

with values from your environment.

```bash
docker exec -e MONGO_ROOT_PASS="$MONGO_ROOT_PASS" unifi-db sh -c \
'mongosh --quiet \
--username root \
--authenticationDatabase admin \
--password "$MONGO_ROOT_PASS" \
unifi \
--eval "
db.networkconf.updateOne(
{
_id:ObjectId(\"NETWORK_OBJECT_ID\"),
site_id:\"SITE_ID\",
name:\"Default\"
},
{
\$set:{
ip_subnet:\"172.16.0.1/24\",
dhcpd_start:\"172.16.0.6\",
dhcpd_stop:\"172.16.0.254\"
}
}
)
"'
```

Expected

```
matchedCount:1

modifiedCount:1
```

